# Aperire fleet trust file, the SHAPE only. Do not copy this into place.
#
# The real file, dashboard/config/fleet-trust.yaml, is written for you. On
# an aggregator, scripts/install-fleet-broker-grant.sh makes this host's key
# when there is no file (and never rewrites one that is there), and
# scripts/aperire-fleet-add.sh makes it the first time a node is joined by
# hand. Pairing places this host's public half on the node. This template
# exists so the shape is documented next to the other config templates, and
# so an operator joining a node on another machine by hand knows exactly
# what to paste.
#
# Two top-level keys, both optional, nothing else:
#
#   private_key   this host's own Ed25519 seed, base64url, no padding. Only
#                 an aggregator has one. It signs the trust bundle, the
#                 knowledge bundle, a model seal job and nothing else, and it
#                 never leaves this host.
#   peers         public keys this host will accept a signature from, one
#                 per line. A node joined to a fleet holds exactly one, under
#                 the fixed label `aggregator`: every signer names that label
#                 as its issuer, and the node looks up that label and no
#                 other.
#
# Owner and mode depend on what it holds:
#
#   with a private_key   the dashboard account's, 0600. Only the dashboard
#                        signs with it, and the Advisor never reads it.
#                        scripts/fleet-trust-split.sh writes
#                        fleet-trust.pub.yaml beside it: the same peers and
#                        a public_key line in place of private_key, root's,
#                        0640 to the group the dashboard and the Advisor
#                        share. The Advisor reads that file to verify every
#                        push. Edit this file, never that one; every
#                        install, update and restore remakes it.
#   peers only (a node)  root's (pairing makes it), 0640 to the group the
#                        dashboard and the Advisor share. The Advisor reads
#                        it where it is.
#
# Wider than 0640 is refused by the tools that touch it.
#
# The parser is strict on purpose: two-space indent under peers, one
# `label: value` per line, bare values, no quotes, no flow syntax. Anything
# else is skipped, and a label that is not found is a plain refusal
# ("no key for aggregator"), never a guess.

# On an aggregator:
#
# private_key: <base64url seed>
# peers: {}

# On a joined node:
#
# peers:
#   aggregator: <base64url public key, printed by aperire-fleet-add.sh>
